Theorem RL-21: program-wide non-atomic RC when no spawn / channel / FFI export

  Preconditions:
    - RL-21 governs program-wide non-atomic RC per Annex E §AIMS
      Non-Atomic RC: "A program with no spawn / channel AND no FFI calls
      exporting Ori-managed pointers -> ALL values thread-local, ALL RC
      non-atomic. FFI included (foreign code may hand a pointer to another
      thread)."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - This is the whole-program corollary of RL-19: if NO thread boundary
      exists anywhere in the program (no spawn, no channel, no FFI export),
      then no value can possibly cross one, so every value is thread-local
      and every RC operation is non-atomic.
    - Shipped: target-system rule; the program-wide spawn / channel / FFI
      inventory is a call-graph property.

  Soundness property:
    Forall program P:

      (P1) Program-wide decision: RL-21 makes ALL RC non-atomic iff P contains
           NO spawn AND NO channel AND NO FFI export.

      (P2) Soundness: with no thread-boundary construct anywhere in P, the
           call-graph derivation (RL-18a / RL-19) classifies every value
           thread-local, so non-atomic RC is correct for every value. The
           presence of ANY one of {spawn, channel, FFI export} reintroduces a
           possible thread boundary, so the program-wide blanket no longer
           applies (per-value RL-19 / RL-20 classification resumes).

    RL-21 refines plain ARC at whole-program scope: a program that never
    spawns a thread, never sends on a channel, and never exports a pointer
    over FFI is provably single-threaded with respect to Ori-managed memory,
    so atomic RC is pure overhead and is eliminated everywhere.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via enumeration over
    the (spawn x channel x FFI-export) presence flags.

    Part (P1/P2) — program-wide flag grid:
      no_concurrency_all_nonatomic -> all non-atomic
      has_spawn_not_all_nonatomic -> NOT all non-atomic
      has_channel_not_all_nonatomic -> NOT all non-atomic
      has_ffi_export_not_all_nonatomic -> NOT all non-atomic
      Coverage gate: 4 program-shape cases — each thread-boundary construct
      independently defeats the program-wide blanket; FFI export is included
      (foreign code may hand the pointer to another thread).

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl21_program_wide_nonatomic;
        program-wide flag enumeration; emits Fail when any thread-boundary
        construct fails to defeat the all-non-atomic blanket)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-21 via the program-wide (spawn x channel x FFI-export) flag grid — all RC non-atomic iff none of spawn / channel / FFI-export is present, with each construct (FFI included) independently defeating the blanket — the whole-program corollary of RL-19 thread-locality
